{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791655446,"nonce":"a0VQ6xOWYaQqTaeUBUn883DDm88=","title":"Read clip-path and the other drawn-but-unread paint from CSS","message":"A clip-path declaration was unread: RenderProps and the display list draw a clip path, but nothing turned the CSS text into one.\n\ncss::clip_path reads none, circle(), ellipse(), inset(), rect(), xywh(), polygon() and path(), with an optional nonzero or evenodd rule, into blinc_core::ClipPath beside its fill rule; PaintWrite::ClipPath carries it. Path data is cut into rings of straight steps (css::svg_path), rings parted by a vertex at 1e30 as the HashLink path constructor does.\n\nStill to read as paint: overflow-fade and backdrop-filter. text-decoration and url() backgrounds need the engine as well.","files":null}]}